# `insta`'s own pending-review file. The `.snap` baseline it is a diff
# against is a checked-in test fixture -- committing it is the entire point
# of a ratchet test (`stdlib_ratchet.rs`, `stdlib_check_ratchet.rs`: "the
# review step is the point, and the ratchet is only meaningful if the diff
# is actually read"). A `.snap.new` is the opposite: uncommitted work in
# progress, exactly like a `.orig` from a patch that failed to apply clean.
#
# This used to also ignore `*.snap` itself, four times over, plus two
# directory-specific rules for the same pattern -- which meant every
# snapshot test's baseline silently never reached git. `cargo test` on a
# fresh clone failed immediately, on every one of them, because the
# baseline they compare against did not exist: confirmed directly by
# removing one and rerunning it. Fixed here, not worked around, because a
# gitignored ratchet is not a ratchet.
*.snap.new

# Built artifacts from the interop example's C caller.
examples/interop/c/main
examples/interop/c/main.exe
